\begin{aligned}\sqrt{5}x+3&=\sqrt{3}x+8\\\sqrt{5}x-\sqrt{3}x&=5\\(\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3})x&=5.\end{aligned}
Dividing each side by \sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3}, and then rationalising the denominator gives
\begin{aligned}x&=\frac{5}{\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3}}\\&=\frac{5}{(\sqrt{5}-\sqrt{3})}\cdot\frac{(\sqrt{5}+\sqrt{3})}{(\sqrt{5}+\sqrt{3})}\\&=\frac{5\sqrt{5}+5\sqrt{3}}{(\sqrt{5})^2-(\sqrt{3})^2}\\&=\frac{5\sqrt{5}+5\sqrt{3}}{5-3}\\&=\frac{5\sqrt{5}+5\sqrt{3}}{2}.\end{aligned}
